===== [76/150]  What is CalColor's code of conduct for parents? =====

Q: What is CalColor's code of conduct for parents?

retrieved: code-of-conduct=0.730, safety-and-materials=0.636, about-overview=0.565, locations-and-contact=0.527

A: CalColor’s Code of Conduct for parents (summary of key points):

- Do not disturb classes or approach teachers or students during class unless it’s an emergency. Pass messages, drinks, or medication through the front desk. Wait in the waiting area or outside until class is dismissed.
- Parents are responsible for on-time drop-off and pick-up; CalColor is not responsible for students before or after their scheduled class. If there’s an emergency or unavoidable delay, contact the studio so staff can care for the child until pickup.
- Arrange any personal meetings with the studio manager through reception.
- Disrespect, defamation, bullying, discrimination, assault, or similar behavior by any parent (or staff/student) will not be tolerated and may lead to a meeting and possible dismissal/expulsion at the studio manager’s discretion.
- CalColor may change teachers or timetables when necessary.
- Studio facilities (classrooms, offices, inventory rooms, etc.) except the lobby are not available for personal use by parents or students.
- Taking photos or brief videos of your own student is allowed; longer videos, invasion of privacy, or theft of intellectual property are not permitted.

