===== [85/150]  How do I know which class level my child should be in? =====

Q: How do I know which class level my child should be in?

retrieved: class-levels=0.562, faq-two-classes-same-level=0.465, faq-potty-trained=0.437, fine-art-kids=0.405

A: Choose the level by your child’s age and skill/experience:

- If age 4–6: Art Exploration (1.5 hrs, 1x/week) — developmental, builds fine motor skills and curiosity.  
- If age 7–9: Art Foundation (1.5 hrs, 1x/week) — fundamentals, styles, vocabulary, teamwork.  
- If age 10–12 (generally 5th grade and up) and experienced: Art Advancement (1.5 hrs, 1x/week) — weekly homework, technical studies, independent research, advanced techniques.  
- If age 8–11 and strongly experienced/passionate: Elite Class — application required (submit best artwork for panel review); 2 hrs, 1x/week.

In addition to age, instructors evaluate skill and readiness (completion of prior level and demonstrated proficiency are considered for advancing). If you’re unsure, contact any CalColor staff for help or book the free trial class for new students to see which level fits.

