===== [95/150]  What's your refund policy if I want my money back? =====

Q: What's your refund policy if I want my money back?

retrieved: cancellation-refund-policy=0.405, faq-refund-missed-class=0.400, summer-camp-pricing=0.365, faq-fsa-receipt=0.304

A: Which program? Our refund rules differ for weekly school-year classes vs. summer camp.

- Weekly school-year classes (auto-renew monthly): To cancel, email the school 30 days (one month) in advance. Missed classes are not refunded; make-up classes are offered instead. If a balance refund is involved, a $20 processing fee applies. You may request a refund within 7 days of your original payment, or request school credit within 14 days of the original payment. No refund or credit is available after 14 days. (Autopay processed by the system is not considered the original payment.)

- Summer camp: Camp refunds are handled by emailing your campus. Timeline:
  - Within 24 hours of payment: full refund, no processing fee.
  - Until April 1: 100% refund minus a $25 processing fee per session.
  - Until May 1: 75% refund (or school credit).
  - Until 2 weeks before camp start: 50% refund (or school credit).
  - Within 2 weeks of camp start: no refund, credit, or camp switch.
  Note: surcharges on card payments (3%) are non‑refundable; bank e-check has no surcharge. The camp refund policy applies in all situations.

If you want us to process a refund or have a specific payment/date to review, please email the front desk at cu@calcolor.com or call (408) 818-8818, or book a free trial at https://calcolor.com/trial.html.

